From afb3c812fe9fc42895e5a88cf7a82ab73dcb0e96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:44:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban/terminal OOM: read the worker log once on
 reclaim; own-scope note keys firm wording on kill exits

Follow-up to PR #2047's review (5888845043, non-blocking nits; card t_01a1d44191cc3cba).

1. `_classify_dead_worker` already reads the whole worker log, but with no
   authority rc and a reap-registry miss `_classify_dead_worker_exit` called
   `_worker_log_exit_code`, which read the whole log a second time inside the
   reclaim write txn. Both helpers now take an optional `log=` (None keeps the
   old self-read), and the reclaim passes the log it holds.
   Test: test_failure_path_reads_the_worker_log_once.

2. `OomWatch._own_scope_note` gave the firm "killed by the OOM killer" wording
   to every non-zero rc, so `cmd | grep` exiting 1 after a pipeline member was
   killed read as the command dying. It now splits like the run-scope path:
   firm wording for SIGKILL (137/-9) and for the SIGTERM (143/-15) systemd sends
   when the survivable scope's default OOMPolicy=stop stops it (the existing
   -15 test keeps its wording); any other rc gets "a pipeline may hide its exit
   status". Tests: test_survivable_non_kill_exit_gets_the_pipeline_wording,
   test_survivable_kill_exit_keeps_the_firm_wording.

3. Docstrings (OomWatch, _own_scope_note): every survivable foreground command
   that finishes, rc 0 included, pays one `journalctl -k` read bounded by
   `since`; a run-scope command reads it only when oom_kill rose.

RED (fix reverted, tests kept): 4 failed (log read twice; rc 1/2/-2 got the
firm wording). GREEN: 17 test files importing the changed code, 243 passed.
